      "message": "This pattern is suspicious.\n\nThe only way for `mCallback` to be null is if the `mExecutor` is null, which is already checked in you runCallbackOnExecutor.\n\nSince registerCallback cannot be called externally, I think we should set `mCallback` and `mExecutor` to be final member of this and remove all the check everywhere instead.\n\n\nThis could be done by merging the constructor and the registerCallback together\n\n\nPlease take this comment as an open discussion, I am not familiar with this code and may be missing something obvious",
